.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the networking applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
They use the Rach2 network stack, which supports IPv4, TCP, UDP, and raw
sockets for root.
IPv6 options in the applets do not provide IPv6 on this kernel.
See
.Xr socketcall 2 .
.Pp
On os-real,
.Xr ping 1
is the project's program, not a BusyBox applet.
The
.Nm httpd
and
.Nm nc
commands also have project implementations on os-simple; see
.Xr nc 1
and
.Xr httpd 8 .
.Bl -tag -width dnsdomainname
.It Nm arp
Display or change the ARP cache.
Rach2 answers the display; the requests that add or delete an entry are not
implemented, so those changes fail.
.It Nm arping
Send ARP requests or replies.
Rach2 has no interval timer, so the
.Dv SIGALRM
that paces the requests and ends a run never arrives:
.Nm arping
sends one request and, unless
.Fl f
ends the run at the first reply, waits until it is interrupted, whatever
.Fl c
and
.Fl w
say.
.It Nm dnsd
Run a small static DNS server.
.It Nm dnsdomainname
Display the DNS domain name.
.It Nm fakeidentd
Provide a fake ident authentication service.
.It Nm ftpd
Serve FTP requests as an inetd service.
Rach2 has no
.Fn chroot
system call, so
.Ar DIR
becomes only the current directory and clients are not confined to it;
the applet falls back to that change whatever its privilege, and it
to it instead.
.It Nm ftpget
Download a file through FTP using TCP.
.It Nm ftpput
Upload a file to an FTP server.
.It Nm hostname
Display or set the host name or DNS domain name.
.It Nm httpd
Listen for incoming HTTP requests.
.It Nm ifconfig
Configure a network interface through the interface ioctls supported by
the kernel.
The kernel does not answer
.Dv SIOCGIFCONF ,
the request that lists the interfaces, so
.Nm ifconfig
fails with no interface named, with
.Fl a ,
and with a name
.Pa /proc/net/dev
does not list; name the interface, as in
.Ic ifconfig eth0 .
.It Nm ifdown
Deconfigure network interfaces.
.It Nm ifup
Configure network interfaces.
.It Nm inetd
Listen for network connections and start programs.
.It Nm ipcalc
Calculate and display network settings from an IP address.
.It Nm nc
Connect to a TCP server or listen for incoming connections.
.It Nm netstat
Display network information, reading
.Pa /proc/net/tcp .
.It Nm nslookup
Query DNS about
.Ar HOST ,
using
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf .
.It Nm ntpd
Run an NTP client or server.
Rach2 has neither the clock-adjusting nor the clock-setting calls the
client uses, so an update of the clock fails;
.Fl w
queries the peers without setting the clock.
.It Nm pscan
Scan
.Ar HOST
and print its open ports.
.It Nm route
Display or edit the kernel routing tables.
The kernel keeps the connected subnet and one default gateway; adding
another route fails.
.It Nm ssl_client
Run the BusyBox SSL client.
.It Nm tcpsvd
Run
.Ar PROG
as a TCP service.
.It Nm telnet
Connect to a telnet server over TCP.
.It Nm telnetd
Handle incoming telnet connections.
.It Nm tftp
Transfer a file to or from a TFTP server.
.It Nm tftpd
Transfer files at the request of a TFTP client.
It is an inetd service and can also run from
.Nm udpsvd .
.It Nm traceroute
Trace the route to
.Ar HOST .
.It Nm udhcpc
Obtain an address through DHCP.
This is how os-real takes its address; the DHCP event script is
.Pa /usr/share/udhcpc/default.script .
.It Nm udpsvd
Bind a UDP socket to
.Ar IP : Ns Ar PORT
and wait for packets.
Run
.Ar PROG
for each packet, redirecting further packets from the same peer address
and port to that program.
.It Nm vconfig
Create and remove virtual Ethernet devices.
Rach2 does not implement the VLAN request, so the operations fail.
.It Nm wget
Retrieve files through HTTP or FTP.
.It Nm whois
Query WHOIS information about
.Ar NAME .
.El
